; AsmParser init is required to emit INLINE ASM — which is how a `:lower (cc/Shim)`
; calling convention is realized (a naked trampoline). Without it LLVM hard-errors
; ("Inline asm not supported by this streamer because we don't have an asm parser
; for this target") and aborts, so every `:shim` cc failed to build on the LLVM path.
(extern LLVMInitializeAArch64AsmParser :cc (cc/C) [] (-> void))

